    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111291" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλομαθ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fond of learning, eager
				after knowledge,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				67b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				82d
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐὰν ᾖς φ., ἔσει πολυμαθής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					1.18
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έστατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.2.1
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλομάθεια</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				376b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				411d
			</span></i>: Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θῶς, ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ant.Diog.
					11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen. rei,
				<i>eager after,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν εἰς τὸν πόλεμον ἔργων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					1.9.5
				</span></i>
			 (
				Sup.
			).</div>
